a:3:{s:4:"time";i:1768940165;s:3:"ttl";i:0;s:4:"data";a:30:{i:0;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"6.0.8";s:4:"date";s:10:"1768117980";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:16:"January 11, 2026";s:5:"notes";s:956:"<ul><li>[Added] Error handling if DataGrab can not initialize a datatype.</li><li>[Added] datagrab_detailed_log config option.</li><li>[Added] Store config option to auto-generate SKUs on import if stock is not defined.</li><li>[Added] Support for Store v6.</li><li>[Improved] Error handling when attempting to fetch local files.</li><li>[Fixed] If csv files with blank headers are found, DataGrab will now randomly assign a heading value.</li><li>[Fixed] Handle missing or duplicate heading names in a CSV file.</li><li>[Fixed] The check for duplicates field was not properly checking against multiple selected fields.</li><li>[Fixed] File import issue when compatibilty mode is enabled.</li><li>[Fixed] Bloqs fields would not import.</li><li>[Fixed] URL Title was not getting updated.</li><li>[Fixed] Store imports will now update existing product modifiers on subsequent imports if the names match and are unchanged.</li><li></li><li></li><li></li></ul>";}i:1;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"6.0.7";s:4:"date";s:10:"1762157040";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:16:"November 3, 2025";s:5:"notes";s:517:"<ul><li>[Added] Cache buster to queue poll request (from Gilbert Lin)</li><li>[Added] Preflight checks to scan json, xml, and csv files for possible encoding or formatting issues that a validator might not see</li><li>[Improved] Support for the Calendar fieldtype imports</li><li>[Fixed] Small issue with legacy CSV import</li><li>[Fixed] Assets fields would not import correctly</li><li>[Fixed] Issue with custom field names of the same value as a DataGrab import setting name when trying to save an import</li></ul>";}i:2;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"6.0.6";s:4:"date";s:10:"1760623980";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:16:"October 16, 2025";s:5:"notes";s:124:"<ul><li>[Added] SEEO Support</li><li>[Fixed] Transcribe and Pages support</li><li>[Improved] Datatype file loading</li></ul>";}i:3;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"6.0.5";s:4:"date";s:10:"1759223280";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:18:"September 30, 2025";s:5:"notes";s:667:"<ul><li>[Added] datagrab_backup_log config item. When enabled the DataGrab-import.log file will be backed up each time a new import is started.</li><li>[Added] datagrab_custom_headers hook.</li><li>[Improved] Import speeds should be much faster. We identified and cached a query that was being repeatedly executed.</li><li>[Fixed] XML import option would not display.</li><li>[Fixed] Remove unnecessary query to fix Low Events imports.</li><li>[Fixed] Low Events field imports.</li><li>[Fixed] Relationship fields were not respecting their assigned channels.</li><li>[Fixed] Fields not configured in the current import were losing previously existed values.</li></ul>";}i:4;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"6.0.3";s:4:"date";s:10:"1757417880";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:17:"September 9, 2025";s:5:"notes";s:665:"<ul><li>[Added] Time Offset option specifically to the Date field - defaults to system timezone.</li><li>[Added] “Running this import” section to import config screen.</li><li>[Fixed] Relationship fields. Add hasFieldValue check to the relationship field file.  Fix the other instances that were returning a boolean when it&#039;s evaluating a strict string.</li><li>[Fixed] Issue with undefined variable.</li><li>[Fixed] Delete old entries setting was not working correctly.</li><li>[Fixed] Some boolean config values were not evaluated correctly cuasing unexpected operations.</li><li>[Fixed] Importer-&gt;setup() now accepts AbstractDataTypeLegacy.</li></ul>";}i:5;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"6.0.2";s:4:"date";s:10:"1753852500";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:13:"July 30, 2025";s:5:"notes";s:2231:"<ul><li>[Changed] PLEASE REVIEW THE UPGRADE GUIDE https://docs.boldminded.com/datagrab/docs/installation-and-upgrading/upgrading-from-5-to-6</li><li>[Changed] Officially requires PHP 8.2 or greater</li><li>[Changed] ee()-&gt;datagrab is dead, long live ee(‘datagrab:Importer’)</li><li>[Changed] All ajw_ prefixes removed from Datagrab’s hooks</li><li>[Changed] The import config settings page UI has received an overhaul</li><li>[Changed] All fieldtype classes updated to support new settings config</li><li>[Improved] DataGrab now works with the Queue module if installed</li><li>[Added] Support for Wordpress export file format, including Advanced Custom Fields</li><li>[Added] Ability to import files directly into the file manager. This introduces a new import type: Entry or File</li><li>[Added] Imported images will now have manipulations applied to them based on the directory they’re imported into, if manipulations are defined.</li><li>[Added] datagrab_clean_filenames config item - strips all special characters when importing a file</li><li>[Added] datagrab_entries_added_count and datagrab_entries_updated_count hooks</li><li>[Added] —force command to override “Update” setting</li><li>[Added] datagrab_use_short_filenames config</li><li>[Added] —params=&quot;productId=123&amp;size=large&quot; option to the import:run command</li><li>[Added] File uploads now support adding values to the description, location, and credit meta data fields</li><li>[Added] Multiple separator options when importing Relationships</li><li>[Added] Bloqs field support</li><li>[Improved] Fluid field support</li><li>[Improved] FIle uploading when a file from a remote URL is appended with a query string</li><li>[Fixed] Calendar to handle timestamps in milliseconds</li><li>[Fixed] Toggle field import</li><li>[Fixed] Using custom fields to check for uniqueness</li><li>[Fixed] Default to title field match if no value is defined</li><li>[Fixed] Endpoint auth settings grid did not display proper text for no results and the add button</li><li>[Removed] Dropped support for Rel (old EE2 style relationship field), Assets, Matrix, Playa, PT Multiselect, Field Pack Checkboxes, MX Google Map, and VMG Chosen Member.</li></ul>";}i:6;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.4.0";s:4:"date";s:10:"1742733840";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:14:"March 23, 2025";s:5:"notes";s:357:"<ul><li>[Added] DataGrab now works with the Queue module if installed.</li><li>[Added] datagrab_custom_headers config option.</li><li>[Fixed] Improve how relationships are found.</li><li>[Fixed] Grids that had a minimum rows setting would throw an error on import even if it had valid rows to import.</li><li>[Fixed] Imports in MSM sites.</li><li></li></ul>";}i:7;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.3.3";s:4:"date";s:10:"1740385800";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:17:"February 24, 2025";s:5:"notes";s:325:"<ul><li>[Added] datagrab_custom_headers config option to allow adding custom headers to each cURL request</li><li>[Fixed] Improve how relationships are found</li><li>[Fixed] Grids that had a minimum rows setting would throw an error on import even if it had valid rows to import</li><li>[Fixed] Imports in MSM sites</li></ul>";}i:8;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.3.2";s:4:"date";s:10:"1737972480";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:16:"January 27, 2025";s:5:"notes";s:162:"<ul><li>[Fixed] Installing DataGrab and upgrading from v3.0.3 would not properly execute all the upgrade scripts resulting in some database query errors</li></ul>";}i:9;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.3.1";s:4:"date";s:10:"1737580800";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:16:"January 22, 2025";s:5:"notes";s:64:"<ul><li>[Fixed] an issue with the 5.3.0 upgrade script</li></ul>";}i:10;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.3.0";s:4:"date";s:10:"1736224980";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:15:"January 6, 2025";s:5:"notes";s:250:"<ul><li>[Added] Endpoints - DataGrab can now accept incoming data from external applications</li><li>[Added] Sidebar navigation.</li><li>[Fixed] Upload destinations for MSM sites were not displaying as options when configuring a file import</li></ul>";}i:11;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.2.4";s:4:"date";s:10:"1731851160";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:17:"November 17, 2024";s:5:"notes";s:286:"<ul><li>[Changed] Fetching CSV files does not verify SSL certificates from import URL similar to JSON file imports.</li><li>[Added] $config[‘datagrab_verify_peer’] = ‘y’; for additional security and to verify SSL host when fetching an import file. Disabled by default.</li></ul>";}i:12;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.2.3";s:4:"date";s:10:"1731342300";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:17:"November 11, 2024";s:5:"notes";s:282:"<ul><li>[Improved] Importing remote files without a file extension</li><li>[Fixed] Make sure the settings are loaded</li><li>[Fixed] Relationship fields inside of Grid now correctly import if Publisher is installed</li><li>[Fixed] Queues if max_execution_time wasn’t set</li></ul>";}i:13;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.2.2";s:4:"date";s:10:"1724057160";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:15:"August 19, 2024";s:5:"notes";s:528:"<ul><li>[Added] additional logging to file importing</li><li>[Fixed] an issue when importing via CLI</li><li>[Fixed] an issue with importing to Simple Grids &amp; Tables fields</li><li>[Fixed] Relationship inside of a Grid field when importing. However, this does not currently work with Publisher installed.</li><li>[Fixed] Force InnoDB engine on the jobs and failed_jobs tables</li><li>[Removed] Some incorrect/excess logging</li><li>[Removed] Licensing validation. Licensing will be handled by expressionengine.com.</li></ul>";}i:14;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.2.1";s:4:"date";s:10:"1706588220";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:16:"January 29, 2024";s:5:"notes";s:245:"<ul><li>[Fixed] The after_channel_entry_save hook gets a full entry data array.</li><li>[Improved] ACT URL based imports should function better, and it&#039;s progress output is prettier.</li><li>[Added] Version check and status update</li></ul>";}i:15;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.2.0";s:4:"date";s:10:"1704299760";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:15:"January 3, 2024";s:5:"notes";s:446:"<ul><li>[Added] When fetching files from remote URLs, you can optionally create the same folder structure in EE</li><li>[Added] Import config file paths and urls can now be set to an environment variable, e.g. $PRODUCTION_IMPORT_URL</li><li>[Added] Simple Grid field import support (except for Heading Rows)</li><li>[Added] Simple Table field import support (except for Heading Rows)</li><li>[Added] Release notes directly in the add-on</li></ul>";}i:16;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.1.1";s:4:"date";s:10:"1701668520";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:16:"December 3, 2023";s:5:"notes";s:612:"<ul><li>[Changed] Unify how the datatypes fetch data. They all use cURL now.</li><li>[Updated] If cURL response is not 200, show the code in the error dialog. Should assist with debugging.</li><li>[Added] Structure parent_title option - if an entry has the requested title it will be set to the parent of an imported item.</li><li>[Fixed] Options dropdown menu was clipped</li><li>[Fixed] CSV with Tab delimiters were not importing</li><li>[Fixed] Structure import settings weren not saving correctly</li><li>[Fixed] Don’t delete exisitng Fluid field data on import if not importing Fluid data. Oops.</li></ul>";}i:17;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.1.0";s:4:"date";s:10:"1696320000";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:15:"October 3, 2023";s:5:"notes";s:509:"<ul><li>[Added] You can now drag and drop reorder the saved imports</li><li>[Added] better messaging when DG can read a file, but can’t find fields to import due to bad configuration</li><li>[Fixed] URL TItle was not properly being used to detect unique entries </li><li>[Fixed] File fields inside of a Grid or File Grid fields can now select sub-folders if using EE 7 and the new File Manager</li><li>[Fixed] If database is on a different port than the default the the queue size query would fail</li></ul>";}i:18;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.0.5";s:4:"date";s:10:"1690444800";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:13:"July 27, 2023";s:5:"notes";s:257:"<ul><li>[Improved] URL Title handling</li><li>[Fixed] PHP 8.1 issue with the Carbon package</li><li>[Fixed] Cloning imports failed due to missing database column default values</li><li>[Fixed] Issues when an import was configured to delete entries</li></ul>";}i:19;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"5.0.3";s:4:"date";s:10:"1687431600";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:13:"June 22, 2023";s:5:"notes";s:506:"<ul><li>[Changed] DataGrab now uses the Laravel Queue library to manage imports.</li><li>[Added] URL Title as a unique field identifier</li><li>[Added] Allow numeric category names option</li><li>[Added] Sub Category delimiter field</li><li>[Added] Assets and Date fields within a Grid field now import correctly</li><li>[Improved] Logging output</li><li>[Improved] Support for the Cartthrob Order Items field type</li><li>[Improved] Support for importing multi-line RTE field data from CSV files</li></ul>";}i:20;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"4.2.2";s:4:"date";s:10:"1677488400";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:17:"February 27, 2023";s:5:"notes";s:635:"<ul><li>[Fixed] Imports should now make unique URL Titles if deemed necessary rather than skip importing the item</li><li>[Fixed] Offset parameter was not working correclty in the CLI command</li><li>[Fixed] First header row in CSV imports was getting imported and causing subsequent import items to be skipped</li><li>[Fixed] CLI Importing was improperly skipping rows</li><li>[Fixed] The new Update Status option was not behaving</li><li>[Fixed] $config[‘datagrab_log_file’] wasn’t properly supported</li><li>[Fixed] JSON files with deeply nested collections can be configured in the path with parent/child/grandchild</li></ul>";}i:21;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"4.2.1";s:4:"date";s:10:"1670544000";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:16:"December 8, 2022";s:5:"notes";s:260:"<ul><li>[Added] —offset parameter to the CLI import command</li><li>[Added] ?batch=no and —batch=no options</li><li>[Fixed] Relationship field imports were not properly ordering related entries</li><li>[Fixed] Re-enable the isUrlTitleUnique check</li></ul>";}i:22;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"4.2.0";s:4:"date";s:10:"1668787200";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:17:"November 18, 2022";s:5:"notes";s:454:"<ul><li>[Added] filename back as a template tag option in run_saved_import</li><li>[Added] Additional options to importing Structure data</li><li>[Added] Update Status option field</li><li>[Added] eecli commands to better handle imports through the command line. You should use these instead of the ACT url when executing imports with cron.</li><li>[Refactor] Move the Structure, Pages, SEO LIte, and Transcribe import methods to their files.  </li></ul>";}i:23;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"4.1.0";s:4:"date";s:10:"1665752400";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:16:"October 14, 2022";s:5:"notes";s:717:"<ul><li>[Added] option to load custom 3rd party datatypes and fieldtypes from folder outside of datagrab</li><li>[Added] Title Suffix and URL Title Suffix configuration options. Lets users choose another value to be appended to the end of the Title and URL TItle fields to create new strings based on 2 values from the import file.</li><li>[Improved] Code reorganization to clean things up.</li><li>[Improved] File uploading logging.</li><li>[Fixed] EE7 - Check for compatibility mode before using {file:X:url}</li><li>[Fixed] PHP 8.1 compatibility issues</li><li>[Fixed] Importing multiple category groups</li><li>[Fixed] Custom fields containing import statuses Open/Closed should now import without error</li></ul>";}i:24;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"4.0.5";s:4:"date";s:10:"1657267200";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:12:"July 8, 2022";s:5:"notes";s:626:"<ul><li>[Added] File Grid field support</li><li>[Added] Option to clone an import</li><li>[Added] Log whenever another add-on is using one of DataGrab&#039;s internal hooks</li><li>[Changed] Sort the configured imports page by name, not it&#039;s ID</li><li>[Fixed] Relationship fields should now import multiple releationships if the entry_ids or titles are separated with the pipe or comma characters, e.g. 2|4|9 or 2,4,9, or Alpha,Beta,Charlie</li><li>[Fixed] Grid insert or update row option</li><li>[Fixed] Relationship assignment during imports by assigning the relationship based on another custom field value</li></ul>";}i:25;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"4.0.4";s:4:"date";s:10:"1652832000";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:12:"May 17, 2022";s:5:"notes";s:279:"<ul><li>[Added] Support for the File Grid fieldtype</li><li>[Fixed] JSON import now displays only unique columns when configuring the import (slight regression from previous release)</li><li>[Fixed] Prevent PHP errors when trying to set PHP config values with php_ini()</li></ul>";}i:26;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"4.0.3";s:4:"date";s:10:"1652169600";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:12:"May 10, 2022";s:5:"notes";s:225:"<ul><li>[Fixed] Entries containing grid fields that should not be modified when importing no longer have their rows deleted</li><li>[Fixed] Issue with importing custom date fields</li><li>[Improved] JSON Import type</li></ul>";}i:27;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"4.0.2";s:4:"date";s:10:"1649084400";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:13:"April 4, 2022";s:5:"notes";s:157:"<ul><li>[Fixed] Issue when importing Relationship fields</li><li>[Fixed] Issue when trying to reset the dev log when there is no existing .log file</li></ul>";}i:28;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"4.0.1";s:4:"date";s:10:"1648549800";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:14:"March 29, 2022";s:5:"notes";s:76:"<ul><li>[Fixed] Incorrect namespacing in the ext.datagrab.php file</li></ul>";}i:29;O:8:"stdClass":5:{s:5:"addon";s:8:"DataGrab";s:7:"version";s:5:"4.0.0";s:4:"date";s:10:"1648540800";s:13:"dateFormatted";s:14:"March 29, 2022";s:5:"notes";s:497:"<ul><li>ExpressionEngine 6 support – UI and functional improvements</li><li>Batch importing now default for all import operations</li><li>Code improvements modernization</li><li>Starting with version 4.0, Datagrab will support ExpressionEngine 6+ only. Older versions of ExpressionEngine are no longer supported.</li><li>Improved error message feedback and vastly improved logging to help with troubleshooting</li><li>Added basic Fluid field support</li><li>Added WordPress import type</li></ul>";}}}